:R-HSA-1296346  a           obo:GO_0071805 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Tandem pore domain K+ channels (K2p) produce leak K+ current which stabilizes negative membrane potential and counter balances depolarization. These channels are regulated by voltage independent mechanisms such as membrane stretch, pH, temperature. Tandem pore domain K+ channels have been classified into six subfamilies; tandem pore domains in weak rectifying K+ channel (TWIK), TWIK-related K+ channel (TREK), TWIK-related acid-sensitive K+ channel (TASK), TWIK-related alkaline pH-activated K+ channel (TALK), tandem pore domain halothane-inhibted K+ channel (THIK), TWIK-releated spinal cord K+ channel)." ;
        rdfs:label          "Tandem pore domain potassium channels" ;
        dc:contributor      "Authored: Mahajan, SS, 2011-05-19" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Edited: Mahajan, SS, 2011-05-23" , "Reviewed: Jassal, Bijay, 2010-09-23" ;
